          {
            "id": "doc_specs",
            "parent_id": null,
            "type": "nodetool.input.StringInput",
            "data": {
              "name": "doc_specs",
              "value": "# Aurora One — Technical Specifications\n\nThe Aurora One is a lightweight urban electric bike. It ships with a 500 Wh removable battery and a 250 W mid-drive motor. The assisted top speed is 25 km/h and the rated range is up to 80 km per charge in eco mode. The complete bike weighs 17 kg and fits riders from 160 cm to 195 cm tall. Frame material is 6061 aluminium; wheel size is 27.5 inches.",
              "description": "Document 1 of your knowledge base"
            },
            "ui_properties": {
              "selected": false,
              "position": {
                "x": 40,
                "y": 400
              },
              "zIndex": 0,
              "width": 300,
              "selectable": true,
              "title": "📄 Doc: Specifications"
            },
            "dynamic_properties": {},
            "dynamic_outputs": {}
          },
          {
            "id": "doc_charging",
            "parent_id": null,
            "type": "nodetool.input.StringInput",
            "data": {
              "name": "doc_charging",
              "value": "# Aurora One — Battery & Charging\n\nThe Aurora One battery charges from empty to full in about 4 hours with the included standard charger, or reaches 80% in roughly 2 hours. An optional fast charger cuts a full charge to about 2.5 hours. The battery is removable, so it can be charged on or off the bike. Aurora recommends storing the battery between 20% and 80% charge when not riding for long periods.",
              "description": "Document 2 of your knowledge base"
            },
            "ui_properties": {
